1:#!/usr/bin/env python3
2:"""ip30abortkill -- RUNG-3 REPRODUCTION ATTEMPT on unmodified `-E sgi -e ip30'.
3:
4:TEST-FIRST: this exists BEFORE any edit, and it is run against the COMMITTED build.  It began
5:as a WITNESS attempt -- if it reproduces, it becomes the witness; if it cannot, the round
6:proceeds documented-only WITH THE ATTEMPT RECORDED, which is a different state from "did not
7:think to ask" and must not render the same.
8:
9:*** IT REPRODUCED, AND IT IS NOW BOTH: the round's WITNESS **and** its SHIPPED DETECTOR.  The
10:sentence above said "not a shipped detector" long after two kill tables had made that false;
11:corrected 2026-09-18. ***  8/21 pre-fix -> 21/21 post-fix on one instrument, then 27 rows after
12:the pass-2 class closure.
13:
14:================================================================================
15:[#566, 2026-10-18 -- a records correction; the text below it is kept as it was written.]
16:The CATCHES list, the fourteen-cell paragraph and "THE CLOSURE IS OWED" below are the 27-row
17:instrument's of 2026-09-18; the DOES NOT CATCH list was updated later and is current.  The
18:probe that ships has 33 rows, and these statements below are no longer true of it:
19:  * the F13 silent-decline repair made both READ arms (0x10020, 0x10028) decline WITHOUT an
20:    announce: there are FOUR announce sites, not six; THREE ISR sites print the shared string,
21:    not five (THE ATTRIBUTION RULE); and `kill 20 rd txt' / `kill 28 rd txt' pin the SILENCE
22:    (want `no');
23:  * `latch 1x' was re-aimed onto the two WRITE arms (0x10020-WR, then 0x10028-WR) when the
24:    read arms went silent;
25:  * THE LATCH-AXIS CLASS CLOSURE, further down, enumerated TEN cells -- {4 announce sites} x
26:    {announce fires, latch sets} + {2 collision directions} -- and rowed them: `latch 1x'
27:    (0x10020-WR), `latch 28wr', `latch 30wr', `latch tick' (ME_nolatchsettick) and `xbit rev'
28:    (MA_assign20wr), each killing its mutant in kill table 4 (32 rows).  V2_assigntick (MD's
29:    shape: the tick's latch set made an assignment) still escaped that table at 32/32, so
30:    `xbit rev2' (ISR -> TICK -> ISR) was added; kill table 5 measured base 33/33,
31:    V1_assign20wr 32/33 and V2_assigntick 32/33 (regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/
32:    killtable4_20260918/, killtable5_20260918/).  MF's cell, a latch set on the 0x10028 READ,
33:    no longer exists;
34:  * the pre-fix red is no longer `13 rows': on this instrument the pre-fix build reds 23 of 33
35:    rows, scoring 10/33 (#566's prefix leg, clause (a): regress/artifacts/ip30abortkill/
36:    gatewire_20261018/legs/probe_prefix.log);
37:  * `Every CATCH below has a MEASURED kill in killtable{,2}' overstates the first CATCH:
38:    reinstating the four abort() calls rests on the PRE-FIX build (clause (a): the 21-row
39:    PREFIX_21row_20260917.out and the 33-row leg above); no table here holds abort()
40:    re-inserted into the FIXED file (clause (b));
41:  * THE CLAIM UNDER TEST quotes the PRE-FIX dev_sgi_ip30.c (`at HEAD' there meant HEAD before
42:    #531), and the row it calls `kill 30 rd' is named `acc 30 rd' in every copy of this probe.
43:Two escapes remain DISCLOSED: MH_nocounter (V7_nocounter, 32/32 in table 4), under MEASURED
